# --- Setup checklist for real Google / Apple sign-in ---
#
# 1. Run sql/profiles.sql in the Supabase SQL editor (adds the `profiles`
#    table this code reads/writes for name, theme, and notification prefs).
#
# 2. Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#    - Site URL: your deployed URL (e.g. https://dome.yourdomain.com), or
#      http://localhost:3000 for local dev.
#    - Redirect URLs: add both the local and deployed origins.
#
# 3. Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Google:
#    - Enable it, paste your Google OAuth Client ID + Secret
#      (from console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials).
#    - Authorized redirect URI to add in Google Cloud Console:
#      https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#
# 4. Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Apple:
#    - Needs a paid Apple Developer account. Create a Services ID + Sign in
#      with Apple key at developer.apple.com, then paste the Services ID,
#      Team ID, Key ID, and private key into Supabase.
#    - Redirect URI is the same Supabase callback URL as above.
#
# Until steps 3/4 are done, the Google/Apple buttons on the login page will
# redirect and then show a Supabase error page — email/password sign-up still
# works fully without any of this.